    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against questionable arms, anchored by our top-scoring options **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **James Wood** (72.56). **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits significantly from the high-floor pairing of a favorable park and a soft matchup against Keller, while **James Wood** continues to flash elite xwOBA metrics, making him an auto-start at the top of the order. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** (66.63) is a strategic lock today; beyond his solid base projection, his score is bolstered by a 100% stolen base expectation against Cecconi\u2014a critical factor given our league's extreme scarcity at the position. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention with a 68.63 score, enjoying a strong setup as the cleanup hitter against Feltner.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Alex Freeland** (37.77) falling just short of the 40.0 efficiency floor required to displace starters. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his matchup against Rasmussen (3.36 xERA) proved too daunting to justify a start, especially when compared to the aggressive offensive profiles of our middle-of-the-order anchors. We are carefully monitoring **Corbin Carroll** (52.12), whose status is currently flagged for risk; his efficiency is suppressed by a difficult L/L matchup against Detmers. While his pure talent typically mandates a start, his current efficiency drop-off is a reminder that we are prioritizing optimization over name value. We remain without the services of **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom continue to occupy IL slots, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining depth in our 5x5 build.",
